					Plu.
					<u>Brut.</u>
					51
				</span></i>
			, etc.; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽ ἕτερα</span>
			<i>at other points</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.42
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			Adv.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτέρως</span></b> 
			<i>in one</i> or <i>the other way</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφοτέρως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				181e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. τε καὶ ἑ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφοτέρως</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				235a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ σκέλους ἑ. ἔχειν,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτεροσκελὴς εἶναι</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				3.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>differently</i>, rarely in Poetry, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐχ ἑ. τις ἐρεῖ</span>”
